# The shadow-oracle TOOL this checkout is judged by. The tool is a separate product
# (GetBusbar/busbar-oracle); everything else in this directory is busbar's own DATA.
#
# WHY A DIGEST AND NOT JUST A TAG. A tag is a name and a name can be moved. The oracle
# decides whether busbar shipped a regression, so the one thing that must not be able to
# change quietly is which judge ran. bin/oracle refuses an archive that does not hash to
# `sha256` below, and harness-rev.sh folds `tag@sha256` into the harness revision — so a
# tool upgrade shows up in every recording made after it, exactly as a recorder change does.
#
# CAVEAT WORTH KNOWING: this is GitHub's auto-generated source archive for the tag. Those
# are stable in practice but are not contractually byte-stable (the compression has changed
# once in GitHub's history). If that ever bites, publish a real release ASSET and pin that
# instead; the shim's check does not care which URL the bytes came from.
#
# To move the pin: bump `tag`, download the archive, and put its sha256 here.
tag=v0.3.15
sha256=2ba70a89ace20cd5e2c6c8e0aae266bc2b8e56a28673e8a60e7f41a0bd0b6ec9
